# Walkthrough — Layer 4 (`shadow_sandbox/reports/`)

Implemented **Layer 4** (`reports/`) of the shadow sandboxing subsystem. This layer is a write-only outcome record generator that formats outcome data produced by Layer 3 (`execution_harness.py`) and saves per-run JSON report files to `shadow_sandbox/reports/<incident_id>_<timestamp>.json`.

---

## Changes Made

### Subsystem Directory: [`shadow_sandbox/reports/`](file:///c:/Users/Shashank/OneDrive/Desktop/Smart%20horizon%20hackathon/ARSE_Final/shadow_sandbox/reports/)

1. **[`report_generator.py`](file:///c:/Users/Shashank/OneDrive/Desktop/Smart%20horizon%20hackathon/ARSE_Final/shadow_sandbox/reports/report_generator.py)**
   - **Role:** Write-only outcome record generator matching Section 5 specifications.
   - **Side-by-Side Preservation:** Generates unique timestamped filenames (`<incident_id>_<timestamp>.json`) with disambiguation counters, guaranteeing zero overwriting of previous runs.
   - **Formatting & Null Semantics:**
     - **BLOCKED cases (`BLOCKED_*`):** Flags `human_intervention_required: true` with a clear message, setting unexecuted stages/timings to `null` (`fault_cleared: null` means "never attempted").
     - **EXECUTED cases (`EXECUTED`):** Flags `human_intervention_required: false` and `message: null`, populating all stage fields and per-stage timing metrics (`safety_check_time_s`, `agent_proposal_time_s`, `guardrail_check_time_s`, `execution_time_s`, `settle_wait_time_s`, `state_recheck_time_s`, `total_pipeline_time_s`).

2. **[`test_reports.py`](file:///c:/Users/Shashank/OneDrive/Desktop/Smart%20horizon%20hackathon/ARSE_Final/shadow_sandbox/reports/test_reports.py)**
   - Unit test suite verifying EXECUTED record formatting, BLOCKED null-field formatting, and non-overwriting file creation.

